      "dark_gray_the_sweetheart_bee_exception": "Dark gray, \"the sweetheart bee\". Exceptional winter hardiness — clusters tight, consumes less honey. Explosive spring buildup. Swarms more when the hive gets crowded.",
      "russian": "Russian",
      "usda_bred_from_primorsky_region_bees_c": "USDA-bred from Primorsky region bees. Co-evolved with varroa for 150 years — strong hygienic behavior. Slower buildup and lower peak honey. Ideal for hands-off IPM.",
      "buckfast": "Buckfast",
      "brother_adam_s_century_long_hybrid_pro": "Brother Adam's century-long hybrid program. Balanced everything: gentle, low-swarm, disease-resistant, productive. No trait is top-tier but none are weak.",
      "saskatraz": "Saskatraz",
      "bred_for_prairie_canada_cold_tolerance": "Bred for prairie Canada: cold tolerance + varroa/tracheal mite resistance. Excellent for cold-climate beekeeping (Maine, Minnesota, Scandinavia).",
      "meadow_old_field": "Meadow / Old Field",
      "open_field_with_mixed_wildflowers_and_": "Open field with mixed wildflowers and clover. The classic apiary site — balanced exposure, easy inspection access, decent forage in all seasons.",
      "forest_edge": "Forest Edge",
      "dappled_shade_with_strong_basswood_lin": "Dappled shade with strong basswood/linden flow in July. Cooler mornings delay first foraging each day. Bears occasionally investigate — consider electric fencing.",
      "urban_rooftop": "Urban Rooftop",
      "park_flowers_ornamental_gardens_no_far": "Park flowers + ornamental gardens + NO farm spray. Heat island makes varroa reproduce faster and crowding raises disease risk. Urban bees actually thrive despite expectations.",
      "coastal_blueberry_barrens": "Coastal Blueberry Barrens",
      "wild_blueberry_barrens_yield_a_massive": "Wild blueberry barrens yield a massive but brief July flow. Salt spray stresses wings; coastal wind cuts foraging on rough days. Year-round mild climate = gentler winters.",
      "mountain_valley": "Mountain Valley",
      "alpine_meadows_bursting_with_wildflowe": "Alpine meadows bursting with wildflowers. Cold nights suppress both disease and varroa. Shorter forage season — build fast or go hungry. Prized for varietal honeys.",
