      "common_core_fluency_automatic_recall_o": "Common Core fluency = automatic recall of basic facts in under 3 seconds. Pizza model for what-out-of-the-whole; bar model for comparison and operation.",
      "compare_cross_multiply_or_benchmark": "Compare — cross-multiply or benchmark",
      "three_tools_same_denom_just_compare_to": "Three tools: same denom (just compare tops), cross-multiplication (a/b vs c/d → ad vs bc), or benchmark to ½ / ¾. Last one is fastest in your head.",
      "operations_add_sub_mul_div_with_rules": "Operations — add/sub/mul/div with rules",
      "add_sub_common_denominator_first_multi": "Add/sub: common denominator first. Multiply: tops×tops, bottoms×bottoms. Divide: keep-change-flip (multiply by reciprocal). Always simplify to lowest terms.",
      "equivalents_same_value_different_form": "Equivalents — same value, different form",
      "multiply_top_and_bottom_by_the_same_nu": "Multiply top AND bottom by the same number; value stays put. ½ = 2/4 = 50/100 = 0.5 = 50%. Equivalent fractions are the bridge between fractions, decimals, and percents.",
      "converter_mixed_improper_decimal": "Converter — mixed ↔ improper ↔ decimal",
      "2_11_4_long_division_gives_a_terminati": "2¾ = 11/4. Long division gives a terminating decimal (denom = 2¹ × 5ⁿ) or a repeating one (any other prime in the denom). 1/3 = 0.333... forever.",
      "wall_visual_proof_of_equivalence": "Wall — visual proof of equivalence",
      "stack_the_fraction_wall_1_whole_2_halv": "Stack the fraction wall: 1 whole = 2 halves = 4 quarters = 8 eighths. Same height = same value. Cuisenaire rods (1952) made this concrete; the wall is the digital descendant.",
