      "weak_lensing_explain": "Background galaxies appear stretched tangentially around the halo. Their shared alignment maps foreground mass, including matter that emits no light.",
      "radio_velocity_guide_title": "Read rotation from the color split",
      "radio_velocity_guide_body": "The 21 cm line shifts blue on the approaching side and red on the receding side. Mapping that shift across the disk reveals both rotation direction and orbital speed.",
      "infrared_transfer_title": "Track absorbed energy",
