      "leonhard_euler_will_give_us_e_i_for_1_": "Leonhard Euler will give us e, i for √(−1), the function-notation f(x), and the Euler formula. Geoboards demonstrate his \"V − E + F = 2\" formula for polyhedra.",
      "friedrich_fr_bel_s_gifts": "Friedrich Fröbel's Gifts",
      "building_on_fr_bel_s_19th_century_kind": "Building on Fröbel's 19th-century kindergarten \"gifts\" (wooden manipulatives), Edith Somervell publishes A Rhythmic Approach to Mathematics — an early manipulative-rich curriculum.",
