      "serial_dilution": "Serial dilution: ",
      "for_very_low_concentrations_dilute_1_1": "For very low concentrations, dilute 1:10 (or 1:100) repeatedly. Each step is precise; cumulative error stays small.",
      "watch_out": "Watch out: ",
      "add_half_the_water_first_then_add_solu": "Add ~half the water FIRST, then add solute + stir until dissolved, THEN top up to the mark. Adding solute to full-volume water often gives wrong final volume due to volume changes during dissolution.",
      "stoichiometry_recipe_math": "⚖ Stoichiometry — recipe math",
      "balanced_equation_mole_ratio_like_a_co": "Balanced equation → mole ratio. Like a cooking recipe, but for atoms. Coefficients tell you the ratio of reactant moles to product moles.",
      "atoms_in_atoms_out_on_each_side_balanc": "Atoms in = atoms out, on each side. Balance metals first, then non-O/H atoms, then O and H last. Charge balanced for ionic equations.",
      "from_coefficients_2_h_1_o_2_h_o_means_": "From coefficients: 2 H₂ + 1 O₂ → 2 H₂O means 2 mol H₂ : 1 mol O₂ : 2 mol H₂O.",
      "mol_g_molar_mass_always_work_in_moles_": "mol = g / molar mass. Always work in moles when comparing across the equation.",
      "for_each_reactant_moles_available_coef": "For each reactant: (moles available) / (coefficient). Smallest result = limiting reactant.",
      "use_limiting_reactant_s_moles_product_": "Use limiting reactant's moles × (product coefficient / limiting coefficient) × product MW.",
      "actual_theoretical_100_real_reactions_": "Actual / Theoretical × 100. Real reactions rarely hit 100% — losses to side reactions, incomplete rxn, transfer losses.",
