      "attack_time_to_reach_full_volume_decay": "Attack: time to reach full volume. Decay: time to fall to sustain. Sustain: held volume level. Release: fade-out time after key release.",
      "a_scale_is_an_ordered_set_of_pitches_m": "A scale is an ordered set of pitches. Modes are rotations of the scale starting on different degrees. Each creates a different emotional mood.",
      "chords_are_built_by_stacking_intervals": "Chords are built by stacking intervals (3rds). Major uses a major 3rd + minor 3rd. Minor reverses them. Extended chords add 7ths, 9ths, and beyond.",
      "kicks_use_a_sine_oscillator_with_a_pit": "Kicks use a sine oscillator with a pitch sweep. Snares combine noise (filtered) + tone body. Hi-hats use high-pass filtered noise bursts.",
      "4_4_4_quarter_note_beats_per_bar_most_": "4/4 = 4 quarter-note beats per bar (most common). 3/4 = waltz feel. 6/8 = compound duple. 5/4 and 7/8 create asymmetric, exotic grooves.",
      "keys_arranged_by_ascending_5ths_clockw": "Keys arranged by ascending 5ths clockwise. Adjacent keys share 6 of 7 notes. Moving clockwise adds sharps; counter-clockwise adds flats.",
      "every_musical_sound_contains_overtones": "Every musical sound contains overtones above the fundamental. Their relative strengths determine timbre — why a trumpet sounds different from a flute at the same pitch.",
      "an_interval_is_the_distance_between_tw": "An interval is the distance between two pitches, measured in semitones. The frequency ratio determines consonance (simple ratios like 3:2 sound smooth).",
      "plays_chord_notes_one_at_a_time_in_seq": "Plays chord notes one at a time in sequence. Up = low to high, Down = high to low. Creates flowing patterns from static chords.",
      "a_filter_removes_frequencies_above_low": "A filter removes frequencies above (lowpass), below (highpass), or around (bandpass) a cutoff frequency. Resonance (Q) amplifies frequencies near cutoff, creating a peak.",
      "tremolo_periodic_volume_changes_amplit": "Tremolo: periodic volume changes (amplitude modulation). Vibrato: periodic pitch changes (frequency modulation). Both controlled by an LFO (Low Frequency Oscillator).",
      "discovered_in_1983_a_noise_burst_feeds": "Discovered in 1983. A noise burst feeds into a very short delay line with feedback. The delay time determines pitch. A filter in the feedback loop controls brightness and decay. Naturally simulates plucked strings.",
      "the_sequencer_is_a_composition_tool_ea": "The sequencer is a composition tool. Each step represents a beat subdivision. The melody row sets pitched notes, drums add rhythm. Musical notation shows what you create.",
