      "frequency_modulation_fm_synthesis_uses": "Frequency Modulation (FM) synthesis uses one oscillator (modulator) to rapidly change the frequency of another (carrier). The modulator:carrier ratio determines the harmonic content. Simple ratios (1:1, 2:1, 3:1) produce harmonic tones. Complex ratios produce metallic, bell-like, or inharmonic sounds. FM was popularized by the Yamaha DX7 in 1983.",
