      "when_the_right_edge_of_a_paragraph_is_": "When the right edge of a paragraph is allowed to fall where it falls, the result is called ragged-right. Each line ends with a natural word break.",
      "justified": "Justified",
      "when_the_right_edge_of_a_paragraph_is__2": "When the right edge of a paragraph is forced to align, the compositor inserts thin metal spacers between words so every line ends at the same position.",
      "compositors_used_metal_quads_between_w": "Compositors used metal \"quads\" between words. The spacing was a craft skill.",
      "same_letter_six_different_times_in_his": "Same letter. Six different times in history. The lowercase a is one of the most-changed letters in Latin type. Compare the closed double-storey \"a\" of medieval Blackletter with the open geometric \"a\" of Helvetica.",
