      "note_on_the_silhouettes_many_of_these_": "Note on the silhouettes: many of these figures (especially the women) have no surviving portraits. The illustrations below are stylized period archetypes that signal era and role, not photographic likenesses. The point is that we know the work; we do not always know the face.",
      "festina_lente_make_haste_but_slowly_a_": "“Festina lente — make haste, but slowly. A pocket book that pirates copy is still my book.”",
      "pioneer_of_portable_octavo_books_dolph": "Pioneer of portable octavo books. Dolphin-and-anchor mark.",
      "the_interest_accrues_whether_you_finis": "“The interest accrues whether you finish the Bible or not. Pay, or the press is mine.”",
      "goldsmith_and_financier_sued_his_colla": "Goldsmith and financier. Sued his collaborator.",
      "master_with_a_tighter_alloy_and_a_slig": "“Master, with a tighter alloy and a slightly smaller body we could fit two more lines per page.”",
      "apprentice_and_later_partner_in_mainz_": "Apprentice and later partner in Mainz. Skilled scribe before he ever set type.",
      "the_shop_carries_my_husband_s_name_the": "“The shop carries my husband’s name. The work carries mine.”",
      "ran_her_press_in_paris_for_nearly_four": "Ran her press in Paris for nearly four decades after her husband’s death.",
      "number_every_verse_a_reader_needs_to_f": "“Number every verse. A reader needs to find their place — and a scholar needs to argue from it.”",
      "multi_generational_scholar_printers_in": "Multi-generational scholar-printers. Introduced verse numbering still used today.",
      "ad_fontes_the_greek_before_the_latin_t": "“Ad fontes. The Greek before the Latin, the Latin before its copies — and let the press carry the original to every desk in Europe at once.”",
      "northern_renaissance_humanist_pushed_p": "Northern Renaissance humanist. Pushed printers to publish ancient texts in their original languages.",
