      "the_master_sends_you_to_fetch_oil_base": "The master sends you to fetch oil-based ink from the cellar. You realize the shop has only enough for half a day. Telling him will mean blame for not noticing earlier. Saying nothing means the press stops at midday.",
      "tell_the_master_immediately_accept_the": "Tell the master immediately, accept the blame.",
      "say_nothing_hope_someone_else_notices": "Say nothing. Hope someone else notices.",
      "run_to_the_supplier_on_your_own_show_i": "Run to the supplier on your own — show initiative.",
      "the_compositor_a_journeyman_three_year": "The compositor — a journeyman three years your senior — drops a galley. The type \"falls in pi\" (becomes a jumbled pile). It will take an hour to sort. He glances at you. He saw you watching. He could blame you.",
      "help_sort_the_type_silently_do_not_say": "Help sort the type silently. Do not say who dropped it.",
      "tell_the_master_what_happened_so_he_kn": "Tell the master what happened so he knows.",
      "pretend_you_did_not_see_stay_out_of_it": "Pretend you did not see. Stay out of it.",
      "you_accidentally_smudge_a_freshly_prin": "You accidentally smudge a freshly printed page. The master is on the other side of the shop. The smudge is small. The page will be inserted into a Bible that costs the buyer 3 years' wages.",
      "tell_the_master_immediately": "Tell the master immediately.",
      "slip_the_smudged_page_under_a_clean_on": "Slip the smudged page under a clean one and hope.",
      "try_to_clean_the_smudge_yourself_with_": "Try to clean the smudge yourself with a damp cloth.",
      "the_shop_closes_at_sunset_another_appr": "The shop closes at sunset. Another apprentice asks if you would help him learn the letter positions in the type case (he is behind). Helping him means staying late. The master prefers apprentices rest so they work fresh tomorrow.",
      "stay_and_help_him_skip_dinner": "Stay and help him. Skip dinner.",
      "suggest_you_both_ask_the_master_if_you": "Suggest you both ask the master if you can use the next slow hour during the day.",
      "tell_him_to_figure_it_out_himself_appr": "Tell him to figure it out himself. Apprentices need rest.",
      "compositor_year_5": "Compositor (Year 5)",
      "a_wealthy_patron_changes_the_order_the": "A wealthy patron changes the order: they want the dedication page set in italic instead of Roman. Your shop has no italic punches. Buying punches takes weeks; the patron expects delivery in three days.",
      "subcontract_the_italic_dedication_page": "Subcontract the italic dedication page to the Aldine Press in Venice (overnight courier).",
      "slant_the_roman_type_slightly_using_sh": "Slant the Roman type slightly using shims. Hope the patron does not notice.",
      "tell_the_patron_honestly_you_cannot_do": "Tell the patron honestly you cannot do italic. Offer Roman instead.",
      "setting_type_for_the_manuscript_you_sp": "Setting type for the manuscript, you spot a clear misspelling — \"recieve\" instead of \"receive.\" The author is dead (a 14th-century theologian). Modern copies all preserve the error.",
      "silently_correct_it_no_one_will_notice": "Silently correct it. No one will notice.",
      "print_the_error_and_add_an_editorial_n": "Print the error and add an editorial note: [recieve, sic].",
      "print_exactly_as_the_manuscript_reads_": "Print exactly as the manuscript reads. Author intent rules.",
      "a_rival_shop_in_cologne_poaches_your_a": "A rival shop in Cologne poaches your apprentice mid-job with better pay. Your typesetting pace drops 30%. The Bible commission is due in two weeks.",
      "hire_a_replacement_immediately_even_if": "Hire a replacement immediately, even if less skilled.",
      "pull_extra_hours_yourself_refuse_to_sl": "Pull extra hours yourself. Refuse to slow the deadline.",
      "tell_the_patron_the_deadline_must_slip": "Tell the patron the deadline must slip by a week. Explain why.",
      "accept_the_recognition_you_earned_it": "Accept the recognition. You earned it.",
      "politely_decline_wait_until_you_are_a_": "Politely decline. Wait until you are a master.",
      "suggest_the_colophon_list_both_your_na": "Suggest the colophon list both your names — master + journeyman.",
      "pressman_year_6": "Pressman (Year 6)",
      "the_platen_has_a_slight_warp_from_yest": "The platen has a slight warp from yesterday's heat. Re-leveling takes 90 minutes. Pressing through means slightly uneven impressions all morning.",
      "re_level_it_lose_90_minutes": "Re-level it. Lose 90 minutes.",
      "push_through_accept_5_lower_quality_th": "Push through. Accept 5% lower quality this morning.",
      "re_level_only_the_parts_that_affect_th": "Re-level only the parts that affect the title page; press through on body text.",
      "ink_supply_is_running_low_sending_the_": "Ink supply is running low. Sending the apprentice to the supplier is risky (he might get the wrong kind, as he did last month). Stopping the press is expensive. Going yourself means abandoning the platen for an hour.",
      "show_the_apprentice_exactly_which_ink_": "Show the apprentice exactly which ink to ask for, give him a sample, send him with the master's seal.",
      "stop_the_press_go_yourself": "Stop the press, go yourself.",
      "stretch_what_you_have_with_a_thinner_b": "Stretch what you have with a thinner blend. Hope it holds.",
      "a_page_comes_out_smudged_the_composito": "A page comes out smudged. The compositor blames the tympan; the master suspects the spacing in the forme. You can feel by hand which is true. Naming the compositor as the cause damages a colleague.",
      "state_the_truth_it_is_the_compositor_s": "State the truth: it is the compositor's spacing. Volunteer to help him correct it.",
      "say_it_is_the_tympan_volunteer_to_reti": "Say it is the tympan. Volunteer to retighten it.",
      "ask_the_master_to_inspect_it_together_": "Ask the master to inspect it together — let him diagnose.",
      "a_typo_is_discovered_on_page_23_of_the": "A typo is discovered on page 23 of the Bible — already printed in 200 copies. Reprinting page 23 means re-setting and re-pressing 200 sheets. Errata slip (a printed correction tucked inside the book) is cheap but sloppy.",
      "reprint_page_23_in_full_insert_the_cor": "Reprint page 23 in full. Insert the corrected page.",
      "insert_a_printed_errata_slip_in_the_fr": "Insert a printed errata slip in the front matter.",
      "ship_as_is_hope_buyers_do_not_notice": "Ship as-is. Hope buyers do not notice.",
      "master_printer": "Master Printer",
      "three_orders_arrive_this_morning_a_a_b": "Three orders arrive this morning. (A) A Bible commission — prestigious, low margin, 6 months of work. (B) An almanac — quick, mass-market, mid margin. (C) A heretical pamphlet — high margin, but printing it could mean Church penalties or worse.",
      "take_the_bible": "Take the Bible.",
      "take_the_almanac": "Take the almanac.",
