      "str": "🧒 · · ·",
      "a_working_day_in_a_1455_print_shop_ran": "A working day in a 1455 print shop ran roughly dawn to dusk, with the highest-skill work in the bright morning hours when daylight made composing and casting easier. The diagram below tracks a representative day.",
      "circular_diagram_of_a_1455_print_shop_": "Circular diagram of a 1455 print-shop working day",
      "shop_day": "shop day",
      "daylight_was_the_constraint_that_shape": "Daylight was the constraint that shaped the day. Bright-hour activities (composing, casting) got the morning; lower-precision work (pressing, drying, hauling) got the afternoon. This pattern stayed roughly the same in print shops for 400 years, until gas lighting (1820s) and then electric (1880s) freed the workday from the sun.",
      "apprenticeship_was_a_legal_contract_no": "Apprenticeship was a legal contract, not a handshake. The text below is a composite drawn from documented 1450-1500 European print-shop apprenticeship contracts (city archives in Frankfurt, Cologne, and Lyon). Names and a few terms are normalized for readability. Annotations on the right explain the period vocabulary.",
      "mainz_the_year_of_our_lord_1457": "Mainz · the year of Our Lord 1457",
      "on_this_day_before_god_and_witnesses": "On this day before God and witnesses, ",
      "master_heinrich_the_printer": "Master Heinrich the printer",
      "householder_of_this_city_has_taken_int": ", householder of this city, has taken into his service ",
      "konrad_son_of_wilhelm_the_cooper": "Konrad, son of Wilhelm the cooper",
      "a_youth_of_twelve_years_to_be_his_appr": ", a youth of twelve years, to be his apprentice in the art and ",
      "of_printing_for_a_term_of": " of printing, for a term of ",
      "seven_full_years": "seven full years",
      "from_this_day": " from this day.",
      "the_master_agrees": "The Master agrees:",
      "to_instruct_the_apprentice_in_casting_": " to instruct the apprentice in casting type, setting type, the working of the press, the mixing of ink, and the keeping of a shop. To furnish ",
      "meat_and_drink_lodging_and_washing": "meat and drink, lodging and washing",
      "and_at_the_end_of_the_term_one_new_sui": ", and at the end of the term one new suit of clothes ",
      "fit_for_a_journeyman": "fit for a journeyman",
      "to_deal_with_the_apprentice_in_good_fa": ". To deal with the apprentice in good faith and not to put him to work beneath the trade.",
      "the_apprentice_agrees": "The apprentice agrees:",
      "to_serve_faithfully_day_and_night_to_k": " to serve faithfully day and night, to keep the secrets of the trade and not reveal them to any rival shop, to ",
      "shun_taverns_and_play": "shun taverns and play",
      "to_take_no_wife_during_the_term_to_obe": ", to take no wife during the term, to obey the Master and his household in all lawful things, and not to absent himself from service without leave.",
      "if_the_apprentice_runs_away": "If the apprentice runs away",
      "or_breaks_this_contract_he_shall_serve": " or breaks this contract, he shall serve double the time absent on his return, and forfeit the clothes promised at the end of the term. If he reveals the trade's secrets, he forfeits all and may be pursued at law.",
      "sworn": "Sworn",
      "by_master_heinrich_by_wilhelm_the_coop": " by Master Heinrich, by Wilhelm the cooper (the apprentice's father, acting for him), and by ",
      "two_witnesses_of_the_guild": "two witnesses of the guild",
      "and_entered_into_the_city_book_by_the_": ", and entered into the city book by the clerk this day.",
      "sealed_with_the_master_s_mark_witnesse": "— Sealed with the Master's mark · witnessed by the Guild of Printers, Mainz",
      "period_vocabulary": "Period vocabulary",
      "discussion_modern_internships_and_trad": "Discussion: Modern internships and trade apprenticeships still inherit pieces of this structure — the term-of-service, the credential at the end, the implicit \"no moonlighting.\" What stays the same; what has changed; what should change?",
      "a_composite_letter_drawn_from_survivin": "A composite letter drawn from surviving 1500s apprentice letters in family archives. The legal contract above is the official voice; this is the apprentice's own.",
      "mainz_the_feast_of_st_lawrence_1455": "Mainz, the Feast of St. Lawrence, 1455",
      "my_dearest_mother": "My dearest mother,",
      "i_write_to_you_in_my_own_hand_which_th": "I write to you in my own hand, which the Master says shows promise, though my fingers still ache from the cold of the morning. The shop is busy with the Bible. I have not seen any of the printed pages up close; the apprentices are not yet trusted to touch them. But I see them stacked under cloth in the back room. There must be thousands. The Master's shop has more books in it now than any cathedral library I have ever heard of.",
      "my_duties_are_sweeping_the_shop_fetchi": "My duties are sweeping the shop, fetching ink from the cellar, carrying lead pigs to the casting room (they weigh as much as a small calf), and watching the journeymen at their work. The compositor, Master Konrad, has begun to let me sort distributed type back into the case. I am slow. He laughs but not unkindly. He says the slow apprentice becomes the careful master.",
      "the_food_is_plain_but_enough_the_maste": "The food is plain but enough. The Master's wife sees that I have bread and broth in the morning and meat at supper. I sleep on a straw mattress with the other apprentice in the loft above the press room. He is from Cologne and snores like a stuck pig.",
      "today_i_dropped_a_tray_not_the_type_th": "Today I dropped a tray. Not the type, thank God, but the wooden tray underneath it. The journeyman pressman did not see, and Master Konrad pretended not to. I will be more careful. The trade is full of dangers I had not thought of when we spoke before I left home: the lead, the boiling oil for the ink, the heavy quoins that can crush a finger. Already I have a small burn on my left hand from the casting room. It is healing.",
      "mother_when_the_work_is_done_at_night_": "Mother, when the work is done at night and the press is quiet, I sometimes go look at the locked-up forme on the imposing stone. The letters are backwards, of course, and at first they made my head ache. But last week I read a full line by myself, reversed and all, and I thought of you and of how I will some day set a page that you could read. I will be a journeyman in six years and a master in ten, the Lord willing. I will print a Bible of my own. You will be proud.",
      "pray_for_me_give_my_love_to_my_sisters": "Pray for me. Give my love to my sisters. Tell Father I am well, and I will write again at Christmas.",
      "your_obedient_and_loving_son": "Your obedient and loving son,",
      "konrad": "Konrad",
      "apprentice_in_the_shop_of_master_heinr": "Apprentice in the shop of Master Heinrich the printer, Mainz",
      "reading_discussion": "Reading discussion",
      "what_does_konrad_reveal_about_apprenti": "What does Konrad reveal about apprenticeship that the contract did not? Where do the two documents agree; where do they differ in tone?",
      "konrad_describes_a_small_burn_and_drop": "Konrad describes a \"small burn\" and dropping a tray. How does he treat these incidents? What does that say about workplace norms?",
      "the_closing_two_paragraphs_shift_from_": "The closing two paragraphs shift from work to home. What does Konrad seem to want most from his mother's reply, and how is that different from what an apprentice in 2026 might want from a parent?",
      "konrad_describes_reading_a_full_line_o": "Konrad describes reading a full line of mirror-reversed type as a milestone. In a 2026 trade apprenticeship (electrical, plumbing, etc.), what would the equivalent \"I did the hard thing once\" milestone be?",
