      "cut_foreign_local_readers_care_more_ab": "Cut foreign — local readers care more about city hall. Wire services can cover foreign.",
      "cut_metro_local_tv_new_digital_news_co": "Cut metro — local TV + new digital news cover city hall. Differentiate via foreign.",
      "cut_both_by_half_try_to_keep_skeleton_": "Cut both by half + try to keep skeleton coverage",
      "refuse_to_cut_journalists_cut_from_pro": "Refuse to cut journalists — cut from production + marketing instead",
      "johann_carolus_had_been_writing_handwr": "Johann Carolus had been writing handwritten newsletters by hand for a small subscription audience (wealthy merchants + diplomats) since the 1590s. By 1604 he had so many subscribers that hand-copying was unsustainable. He bought a press, started printing the newsletter as the Relation, and petitioned the Strasbourg city council in late 1605 for a printing monopoly. The petition (which survives) is the founding document of the newspaper as a form.",
      "within_20_years_similar_papers_had_app": "Within 20 years similar papers had appeared in Wolfenbüttel (1609), Amsterdam (1618), London (1622), Cologne (1620), Berlin (1626), Hamburg (1630), Stockholm (1645), and Boston (1704). The form spread fast once one printer had proven it worked.",
      "sample_headlines_from_this_paper": "— Sample headlines from this paper —",
      "interesting": "🔍 Interesting: ",
