      "anna_r_gerin": "Anna Rügerin",
      "aldus_manutius_3": "Aldus Manutius",
      "klaus_a_17_year_old_senior_apprentice_": "Klaus, a 17-year-old senior apprentice, has been short-changing you on lunch + giving you the worst chores. You discover he is also stealing small amounts of paper to sell. What do you do?",
      "tell_the_master_directly": "Tell the master directly",
      "confront_klaus_privately": "Confront Klaus privately",
      "endure_quietly_eat_less_work_harder": "Endure quietly. Eat less + work harder.",
      "quietly_take_a_small_share_of_the_pape": "Quietly take a small share of the paper sales",
      "a_wealthy_customer_a_city_notary_asks_": "A wealthy customer (a city notary) asks you to bring extra ink to his manuscript shop \"off the books\" — he tips you a florin to do so. The master would punish you if he knew.",
      "take_the_tip_bring_the_ink_quietly": "Take the tip + bring the ink quietly",
      "refuse_explain_you_cannot_do_this": "Refuse — explain you cannot do this",
      "tell_the_master_about_the_offer": "Tell the master about the offer",
      "you_set_the_type_for_a_200_page_latin_": "You set the type for a 200-page Latin grammar. After the first 50 pages are printed, you discover a typo on page 38 — \"amat\" should be \"amet.\" Reprinting 50 pages costs the master 2 florins in paper + 2 days of labor. The error is small (a tense difference) + might be missed in proofing.",
      "confess_immediately_accept_the_cost": "Confess immediately + accept the cost",
      "hide_the_typo_hope_no_one_notices": "Hide the typo + hope no one notices",
      "fix_in_remaining_copies_say_nothing_ab": "Fix in remaining copies, say nothing about the printed 50",
      "anna_a_17_year_old_baker_s_daughter_si": "Anna, a 17-year-old baker's daughter, signals interest in walking with you. But apprentices are forbidden to court or marry by guild rules. If caught, you lose 6 months of progress.",
      "court_her_secretly": "Court her secretly",
      "tell_her_you_cannot_until_your_apprent": "Tell her you cannot until your apprenticeship ends",
      "pursue_openly_accept_consequences": "Pursue openly + accept consequences",
      "a_wealthier_rival_print_shop_in_the_sa": "A wealthier rival print shop in the same city offers to poach you — they will pay you a small wage (your master pays you nothing yet) + complete your training. Leaving breaches your contract; the rival shop swears the master won't find out.",
      "leave_for_the_rival": "Leave for the rival",
      "stay_loyal_to_your_master": "Stay loyal to your master",
      "tell_your_master_negotiate_for_actual_": "Tell your master + negotiate for actual wages",
      "your_master_is_taking_on_a_greek_latin": "Your master is taking on a Greek-Latin edition (rare + prestigious). He needs help with Greek typesetting. Greek type is brutal — different letterforms, more ligatures, longer hours. Mastering it would set you apart. Or you could relax in the evenings with the other apprentices at the tavern.",
      "volunteer_for_the_greek_work_extra_unp": "Volunteer for the Greek work — extra unpaid hours",
      "maintain_social_ties_go_to_the_tavern": "Maintain social ties — go to the tavern",
      "take_on_some_greek_work_but_not_all_ev": "Take on some Greek work — but not all evenings",
      "a_florentine_scholar_commissions_a_400": "A Florentine scholar commissions a 400-page Latin edition — 4-month project, premium pay. The master wants to assign you as lead compositor. You've never done a commission this size. Mistakes will be expensive + visible. Decline + the work goes to the senior apprentice.",
      "accept_the_commission": "Accept the commission",
      "decline_suggest_the_senior_apprentice": "Decline + suggest the senior apprentice",
      "accept_ask_the_master_for_ongoing_guid": "Accept + ask the master for ongoing guidance",
      "the_local_printers_guild_holds_an_annu": "The local printers' guild holds an annual dinner. Your master takes you for the first time. Drinks flow. A master from a rival shop praises your Greek work + offers to introduce you to a Frankfurt printer for future contacts. He also asks you to share a few details about your master's commissions. The \"few details\" are not damaging but they are guild gossip you should not share.",
      "share_the_details_it_s_just_gossip": "Share the details — it's just gossip",
      "politely_refuse_to_share": "Politely refuse to share",
      "talk_only_about_your_own_greek_work_no": "Talk only about your own Greek work, not the master's commissions",
      "your_master_gives_you_the_choice_of_wh": "Your master gives you the choice of which area to deepen for your final two years.",
      "composition_typography_will_become_a_c": "Composition + typography (will become a compositor for life)",
      "presswork_ink_will_become_a_pressman_h": "Presswork + ink (will become a pressman, hands-on, hard physical labor)",
      "business_arithmetic_will_become_a_shop": "Business + arithmetic (will become a shop foreman or own a shop)",
      "a_cologne_customer_wants_a_heretical_t": "A Cologne customer wants a heretical theological tract printed (denying purgatory). The master is hesitant — the work pays well but could attract church inquiry. He asks your opinion.",
      "take_the_commission_money_is_money": "\"Take the commission — money is money\"",
      "decline_too_risky": "\"Decline — too risky\"",
      "take_it_but_use_a_fake_imprint": "\"Take it but use a fake imprint\"",
      "you_must_produce_a_journeyman_piece_a_": "You must produce a journeyman piece — a printed work that demonstrates your full skill. What do you choose?",
      "a_small_psalter_psalm_book_in_latin_wi": "A small psalter (psalm book) in Latin with red-and-black initials",
      "a_small_greek_latin_edition_of_an_aeso": "A small Greek-Latin edition of an Aesop fable",
      "a_vernacular_german_ballad_with_woodcu": "A vernacular German ballad with woodcut illustration",
      "a_single_broadside_political_poem_agai": "A single broadside political poem against a corrupt local official",
