      "you_qualify_as_a_journeyman_what_now_t": "You qualify as a journeyman. What now? (This decision shapes your career.)",
      "stay_with_your_master_as_a_paid_journe": "Stay with your master as a paid journeyman",
      "travel_as_a_wandering_journeyman_acros": "Travel as a wandering journeyman across Europe",
      "open_your_own_shop_immediately": "Open your own shop immediately",
      "marry_the_daughter_of_a_master_printer": "Marry the daughter of a master printer + inherit a shop",
      "you_become_a_senior_journeyman_then_fo": "You become a senior journeyman, then foreman of your master's shop",
      "eight_years_after_qualifying_you_are_t": "Eight years after qualifying you are the trusted foreman. Your master makes you a partial partner. When he dies in 1502 you inherit a share + keep the shop running with his widow until she remarries. Comfortable, respected, never famous. Your name is in one surviving guild ledger.",
      "your_wanderjahre_take_you_across_europ": "Your wanderjahre take you across Europe — and shape your career",
      "you_work_in_augsburg_nuremberg_frankfu": "You work in Augsburg, Nuremberg, Frankfurt, Lyon, Venice over 3 years. You see many shops + meet many printers. When you finally settle (at 24), you have unmatched practical knowledge. You open a small shop in your home city + specialize in the unusual genre you discovered abroad.",
      "you_open_your_own_shop_at_21_a_long_ha": "You open your own shop at 21 — a long, hard climb",
      "the_first_3_years_are_brutal_you_sleep": "The first 3 years are brutal. You sleep at the shop. You make business mistakes that nearly bankrupt you. But by year 5 you have a customer base. By year 10 you are profitable. Your shop runs for 35 years. You teach 8 apprentices yourself. One of them becomes more famous than you.",
      "you_marry_into_ownership_and_prove_you": "You marry into ownership — and prove yourself fast",
      "you_marry_lena_daughter_of_master_prin": "You marry Lena, daughter of master printer Konrad Müller. Within 2 years his health fails + you take over the shop. The trade grumbles about how you got there. Within 5 years your work speaks for itself + the grumbling fades. You run a successful shop for 30 years + your children inherit.",
      "each_master_offers_different_training_": "Each master offers different training, different working conditions, different opportunities. Read carefully. Once you choose you cannot change.",
