      "about_apprenticeship_in_1480": "📜 About apprenticeship in 1480",
      "a_typical_printer_s_apprenticeship_las": "A typical printer's apprenticeship lasted 7 years (varied by city + guild). Apprentices started 12-16, lived with the master, received no wages but bed + board + training. Master could whip, fine, or extend contracts for disobedience. Marriage forbidden until journeyman status. After 7 years apprentices presented their journeyman piece + were tested by the guild. Successful apprentices became journeymen — wage-earning craftsmen who could travel + work — and eventually masters with their own shops.",
