      "in_1962_roger_payne_placed_a_barn_owl_": "In 1962, Roger Payne placed a barn owl in a totally dark room with a mouse on a leaf-litter floor. The owl could hear the leaves rustle but see nothing. He recorded ~17 silent strikes — every one a kill, accurate to ~1° elevation + azimuth. This works because barn owls have ",
