      "three_phases": "Three phases",
      "maine_gdl_learner_s_permit_at_15_w_dri": "Maine GDL: Learner's Permit at 15 with driver's ed for applicants under 18. Intermediate License at 16 after holding the permit 6+ months and logging 70 supervised hours. Passenger, curfew, and device restrictions last 270 days and can extend if violated.",
      "70_supervised_hours": "70 supervised hours",
      "before_the_road_test_maine_requires_70": "Before a license for an applicant under 21, Maine requires 70 hours of supervised driving, including 10 at night. These hours get certified on the driving log before the road test.",
      "phones_zero_tolerance": "Phones — zero tolerance",
      "under_18_all_mobile_device_use_is_bann": "Under 18: all mobile-device interaction is banned while driving, including hands-free and GPS input. During the intermediate period, violations can bring a $250-$500 fine, a 60-day first-offense suspension, and another 270 days of restrictions.",
      "the_clock_resets": "The clock resets",
      "a_moving_violation_conviction_during_i": "An intermediate-license restriction violation extends your passenger, curfew, and device restrictions by another 270 days. It can also mean a $250-$500 fine and license suspension.",
