      "top_of_headrest_even_with_the_top_of_y": "Top of headrest even with the TOP of your head — not your neck.",
      "the_headrest_is_actually_a_head_restra": "The headrest is actually a HEAD restraint — it catches your HEAD in a rear-end collision. Raise it until its top is level with the crown of your head. The face should be no more than 4 inches from the back of your head.",
      "level_w_head_top": "← level w/ head top",
      "step_4_steering_wheel_position": "Step 4: Steering Wheel Position",
      "wheel_10_12_inches_from_chest_hands_at": "Wheel 10-12 inches from chest. Hands at 9 and 3 o'clock.",
      "with_a_straight_back_your_wrist_should": "With a straight back, your wrist should rest on the TOP of the wheel when your arm is fully extended. That gives you 10-12 inches clearance to your chest — enough for the airbag to deploy without slamming into you.",
