      "doubling_your_takeoff_speed_quadruples": "Doubling your takeoff speed quadruples your range — same as pumping in the halfpipe. That's why pros sprint hard at gaps.",
      "peak_height_2": "Peak height: ",
      "h_peak_v_sin_2g_at_30_and_15_mph_you_p": "h_peak = (v · sinθ)² / (2g). At 30° and 15 mph you peak ~3 ft above takeoff; at 45° you peak ~6 ft. More vertical means more time to spot the landing.",
